  "response_text": "The PSP (Process Stack Pointer) points to the memory location of where the thread\u2019s stack exists. Before running a thread, we will need to switch modes using the __set_PSP function so that the CPU will use the expected memory location required to run threads. If the __set_PSP function wasn\u2019t called, the CPU will try to access invalid memory locations or even dereference a NULL pointer and will result in a hard fault and crash the program. Setting the PSP ensures that the thread has a valid stack to use for local variables, context saving, and return addresses.\\n",
